    ['id' => 'remote', 'title' => 'Remote support contracts', 'body' => [
      'One contract per vessel and period: the hours included, the response time, the coverage hours and how we connect. Tickets raised on the vessel are covered by the live contract and every remote session is logged against it.',
      'An end date creates the renewal task, due the agreed number of days before the end; a contract without an end date is open-ended and has no renewal reminder.',
      'The log of a document is folded (v1.198.2): the card "Log" (also named "History" or "Audit trail") at the bottom of a document page — purchase order, requisition, BOM, supplier invoice and payment request, production order, system budget, offer, ticket, timesheet, job order, activity report, task, ISO / IT record, assessment, recruitment application — is now closed when the page opens, so the page is shorter. Click the title (the + on the right) to open it; nothing is removed and everything is still recorded as before.',
      'Speed — Dashboard, KPIs, Cash flow, projects list and HR pages (v1.198.1): the health report of 19 November showed the Dashboard taking up to four seconds with about 4 300 database statements whenever the KPI cockpit was renewed, and the projects list and the HR dashboard asking several hundred. The cause was that the budget and KPI figures were asked sub-project by sub-project (13 statements each). They are now read for all sub-projects together in about a dozen statements, and the same was done for the per-project figures of the projects list (offers, footprint, open tickets, permits), the KPI trends, the cash-flow forecast, the people online, and the people list of the HR pages (it was read up to fifteen times per page). Nothing changes in what the pages show — the numbers were compared before and after and are identical. In the test copy with 150 projects the Dashboard went from about 6 400 statements to about 220, KPIs and the KPI report from about 8 000 and 6 300 to about 100, Cash flow from 2 600 to 60, and the projects list was halved. The remaining lines of "Slow statements" are single simple statements that waited on the hosting database for 0,1–0,3 s; they are not caused by the portal. The line "[ar_old] … made internal" under PHP errors is an information message of the report filing, not an error.',
      'Filters — type to pick from the list (v1.195.3): a drop-down became a type-to-search list only when it had more than eight entries, so a short filter such as Vessel on the purchase orders opened as a plain list. Now, in every filter bar of the portal, a drop-down with four or more entries opens with a search box: click it, type a few letters, press Enter or click the entry. The Vessel and Supplier filters of Purchase orders and of the Pipeline board are always searchable, whatever their length. Fixed choices of two or three entries (for example Purpose) stay plain lists.',
      'Equipment given to employees (v1.189.0): the members of the IT & Cybersecurity team have HR › Equipment to give. Choose the employee and prepare what he or she receives from IT — computer, telephone / SIM, keys / cards / badge; hardware of the asset inventory can be picked from the list (description and number are filled in, and one asset cannot be given to two people). HR is notified and puts your lines on the issue list the employee accepts. You see only the lines of your categories, not the HR card. The asset record then shows "held by …"; when the employee hands the equipment back and HR accepts it, the asset is free again.',
      'Daily health report — three corrections (v1.177.1): (1) "Database steps: GAS-CP-R46-005" was a false alarm of the check itself — the step had been applied; it now reads the column correctly. (2) "Update backups": the daily house-keeping keeps the last three backup folders and now really removes the older ones (they contain sub-folders, which the old clean-up could not empty); the warning disappears after the next night. (3) Slow pages: the Projects list ran several thousand database statements per view because of per-sub-project calculations; see the line "statements per page" of the next reports to follow the effect.',
      'Subscriptions (v1.167.0): a contract is also the subscription of the customer. Besides the period it carries the product (Mb Connect, FortiGate …) with its serial number, the renewal period (1 year, 3 years …), the date installed, the payment status (Ongoing, Pending payment, Paid by customer, Rejected by customer, Subscription expired), the licence expiry of the device and the SQ / offer number it was sold with.',
      'What runs out: the five numbers above the list — active subscriptions (with those pending payment), renewal within 30 days, renewal within 90 days, licences running out within 90 days, and expired and not renewed — open the list filtered. The list has a column Licence expiry; a date within 90 days is gold, a passed one red. The status filter adds Renewal within 90 days, Licence runs out within 90 days and To renew — no renewal offer yet.',
      'Import: under the filters, Import subscriptions from the list of Sales takes the .csv or .xlsx with the columns Vessel, SQ, Product, Subscription details, Payment Status, Renewal Period, Renewal Date, Date Installed, Price, Serial Number, Expiry Date. The vessel is found by its name (M/Y, S/Y … ignored; former names count); tick Create the vessels that are not in the portal to add missing ones, otherwise those rows are listed and skipped. A row without a vessel is skipped. Rejected by customer becomes Cancelled, Subscription expired or a renewal date in the past becomes Expired, everything else Active with its renewal task. A subscription already there (same vessel, SQ and product) is skipped, so the file can be uploaded again. Imported subscriptions are internal — set Visibility to the customer on those the customer should see. Import, renewal offer and renewal are for administrators, management and staff who see the offers.',
      'Sales: the subscription page has a block Sales — the offer it was sold with (linked when the SQ or offer number is among the offers of the portal) and the renewal offer. + Renewal offer, with a project of the vessel chosen, creates a draft offer in Commercial › Offers titled Renewal — plan — vessel (period), with the fee of the subscription as amount and the new period in the notes; complete and send it there — from then on it stands in the sales pipeline. The offer page shows the subscription it belongs to. When the customer accepts, Renew for another period moves the end date forward by the renewal period, sets the payment status to Ongoing, makes the renewal offer the offer of the subscription and writes a line in the internal notes; the renewal task moves with the new end date.',
      'Weekly e-mail to Sales (v1.168.0): once a week, from Monday, the people marked Sales (Settings › Users) and management receive by e-mail and as a notification the subscriptions to renew — running out within 90 days or lapsed in the last 180 days, with the renewal offer if there is one — and the licences running out within 90 days. Nothing is sent in a week when nothing runs out; accounts without financial data are left out. Under the filters of the list, Weekly e-mail to Sales shows whether it is on, with Send now; management turns it off or on there.',
